{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1551611-character-building-for-an-upcoming-game","id":1551611,"title":"Character Building for an upcoming game","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted","Solar Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2025-06-11T20:43:12-07:00","id":1551611,"title":"Character Building for an upcoming game","content":"Aloha!<br /> <br /> Gist: I'm making a Twilight bent on &quot;redeeming&quot; the Yozis by trying to force their Demons to create Exigents. This has little to actually do with redeeming them, he's just trying to Syndrome-from-Incredibles the Dragonblooded (because eff them that's why). <br /> <br /> Given the # of Charm revisions for Solars, let me begin by requesting 0 redirection to homebrew. I believe the ST is attempting to run by the book. That said, here are some questions:<br /> <br /> Disclaimer: I sometimes become recognition blind, like I read something 100 times and miss a key bit every time until someone points it out to me. My apologies if answers to any of these are already explicit in the book somewhere.<br /> <br /> 1. Can I have multiple Familiars? It seems like yes. The merit says it can be repurchased, but I'm not sure if that's supposed to mean you replace a dead or released familiar. Even with that in mind, I think by explicit RAW I can have at least 2+ Essence (1 from Merit, 1 from Ephemeral Induction Occult Capstone) and Essence from Twilight Anima.<br /> <br /> 1.1 With multiple familiars in play, is the survival charm Deadly Onslaught Coordination understood to be cheese, or standard operating procedure for a favored Survival Solar? It feels like you can use it to easily stack onslaught penalties on a target before you swoop in with a decisive attack.<br /> <br /> 2. Brawl's Falling Hammer Strike: does that only apply to onslaught penalties from the Solar's attacks, or just the target's current total Onslaught penalty?<br /> <br /> 2.1 Does Brawl have an equivalent to Glorious Solar Sabre/Golden Bow? <br /> <br /> 3. Terrestrial Spell: Summon Elemental, does this have an effect if it is your Control Spell? I think it's the only one lacking an entry.<br /> <br /> I'm sure I'll have more as we go. Any input is appreciated, thanks!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28845-matt_c","name":"Matt_C","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":1,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-06-12T00:02:28-07:00","id":1551618,"title":"","content":"I\u2019m currently away from my books, but it\u2019s intentional that Demon of the First Circle and Summon Elemental lack a Control Spell bonus.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-06-12T18:21:12-07:00","id":1551644,"title":"","content":"Any insight into why is appreciated.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28845-matt_c","name":"Matt_C","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":1,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-06-13T00:05:20-07:00","id":1551647,"title":"","content":"I think it was stated that those two summons spells are just kind of too versatile to have a control effect. Basically because due to the plethora of ways to use them, both what you summon and duration, it was just too much of a problem to come up with a satisfactory effect that would be thematically appropriate and not have heavy risk of breaking things. <br /> <br /> 2) Falling Hammer: Okay so based on the example the way my group interpreted it is that the user's onslaught against the person doesn't reset. So if our brawler and the target are fighting and the brawler keeps using the hammer then it just ticks up every round the charm works. If the brawler and spearman are taking shots at the same person, then the spearman's onslaught falls off at reset. So the target would reset 2-&gt;1 because the hammer stops the brawler's from falling. But the brawler does it again and the climb continues. <br /> <br /> 2.1) Not really since brawl kind of tends to be playing off being unarmed, so brawl focused more on making your hands and feet more dangerous when you strike someone as the perk of brawl is disarming only works via puns as opposed to a melee combatant or archer who might lose access to their weapon. <br /> <br /> 3","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-06-13T19:15:20-07:00","id":1551669,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nalak42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1551611-character-building-for-an-upcoming-game?p=1551647#post1551647\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think it was stated that those two summons spells are just kind of too versatile to have a control effect. Basically because due to the plethora of ways to use them, both what you summon and duration, it was just too much of a problem to come up with a satisfactory effect that would be thematically appropriate and not have heavy risk of breaking things.<br /> <br /> 2) Falling Hammer: Okay so based on the example the way my group interpreted it is that the user's onslaught against the person doesn't reset. So if our brawler and the target are fighting and the brawler keeps using the hammer then it just ticks up every round the charm works. If the brawler and spearman are taking shots at the same person, then the spearman's onslaught falls off at reset. So the target would reset 2-&gt;1 because the hammer stops the brawler's from falling. But the brawler does it again and the climb continues.<br /> <br /> 2.1) Not really since brawl kind of tends to be playing off being unarmed, so brawl focused more on making your hands and feet more dangerous when you strike someone as the perk of brawl is disarming only works via puns as opposed to a melee combatant or archer who might lose access to their weapon.<br /> <br /> 3</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks! That helps.<br /> <br /> I'll continue tweaking but I figure since we have a couple months before game start I'm going to try and redux a MA I homebrewed for 1e based on Puppetry. I'll post that in a separate thread.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28845-matt_c","name":"Matt_C","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":1,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}